content.text:
I put a full Peachify integration in your workspace under `src/peachify/` (TypeScript core), `src/components/PeachifyPlayer.tsx` (React), and `src/peachify/peachify-vanilla.js` (no build step).

## What you get

| Module | Role |
|--------|------|
| `buildEmbedUrl.ts` | Builds movie/TV URLs, all query params, hide controls, TMDB/`tt` IDs |
| `PeachifyController.ts` | `postMessage` control + `PLAYER_EVENT` / `MEDIA_DATA` listener |
| `progressStorage.ts` | Load/merge/save `peachifyProgress` in `localStorage` |
| `getResumeSeconds()` | Resume from stored progress (skips last ~30s) |
| `PeachifyPlayer.tsx` | React iframe with auto-resume + ref API |
| `peachify-vanilla.js` | Same behavior for plain HTML |

## Quick usage

### React

```tsx
import { PeachifyPlayer } from './components/PeachifyPlayer';

<PeachifyPlayer
  target={{
    type: 'tv',
    mediaId: 76479,        // or "tt1190634"
    season: 1,
    episode: 1,
    options: {
      sub: 'English',
      quality: '1080',
      startAt: 120,        // optional; autoResume fills from localStorage if omitted
      accent: 'B54666',
      autoNext: true,
      servers: false,      // hide control
    },
  }}
  autoResume
  onMediaData={(store) => { /* full progress object saved automatically */ }}
  onPlayerEvent={({ event, currentTime, duration }) => {
    if (event === 'ended') { /* next episode */ }
  }}
/>
```

Ref controls: `playerRef.current?.play()`, `.pause()`, `.seek(300)`, `.setVolume(0.8)`, etc.

### Vanilla JS

```javascript
const { mountPeachifyPlayer } = window.Peachify;

const { controller } = mountPeachifyPlayer(
  document.getElementById('player'),
  {
    type: 'movie',
    mediaId: 786892,
    options: { dub: 'English', quality: '1080p' },
  },
  { autoResume: true }
);

controller.play();
controller.seek(300);
```

Open `examples/watch-page.html` in a browser (serve over HTTP so the iframe loads) for a working demo.

## Security & sync behavior

- Incoming messages are filtered by `event.origin === 'https://peachify.top'` and `event.source === iframe.contentWindow`.
- Outbound commands use `postMessage(..., 'https://peachify.top')` (stricter than `'*'`, same target).
- `MEDIA_DATA` is merged into `localStorage` under `peachifyProgress` (configurable).
- `timeupdate` callbacks are throttled to 1s by default to avoid UI churn.

## URL examples the builder produces

- Movie: `https://peachify.top/embed/movie/786892?sub=English&quality=1080&startAt=8726`
- TV: `https://peachify.top/embed/tv/76479/1/1?autoNext=true&showNextBtn=true&accent=B54666`

Copy `src/peachify` and `src/components/PeachifyPlayer.tsx` into your streaming app, or use the vanilla script directly. If you tell me your stack (Next.js, Nuxt, Svelte, etc.), I can adapt the component to match it.

